{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFYBKk8DComyEo6WDRrV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013bJZq2A6ULypsZFmHwTERt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat docs/adr/0001*.md; sed -n 1,70p skill/scripts/route_check.py; sed -n 60,100p skill/scripts/tiiny_ctl.py; sed -n 205,235p skill/scripts/tiiny_ctl.py; sed -n 455,500p skill/scripts/tiiny_ctl.py; sed -n 175,200p skill/plugin/__init__.py; ls .scratch; ls .scratch/* | head"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4404,"cache_read_input_tokens":46883,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4404},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fa7ddb5-486f-4c1d-8d10-e98d3ec44829","uuid":"0bea244e-c656-4355-82c8-2c8808f37bfa","timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:41:34.820Z","request_id":"req_011ChFYBKJpwoztaigqP1HmT","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_013bJZq2A6ULypsZFmHwTERt":{"command":"cd /Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory && cat docs/adr/0001*.md; sed -n 1,70p skill/scripts/route_check.py; sed -n 60,100p skill/scripts/tiiny_ctl.py; sed -n 205,235p skill/scripts/tiiny_ctl.py; sed -n 455,500p skill/scripts/tiiny_ctl.py; sed -n 175,200p skill/plugin/__init__.py; ls .scratch; ls .scratch/* | head"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_013bJZq2A6ULypsZFmHwTERt":{"cwd":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013bJZq2A6ULypsZFmHwTERt","type":"tool_result","content":"# Ship as one Hermes user plugin directory, installed by npm\n\n**Status:** Accepted (2026-11-20)\n\n## Context\n\nThe routing backend, the controller and the skill are Python and Markdown\nthat run inside, or alongside, the Hermes harness. Before this decision they\nwere installed by hand into three places: the routing backend into the\nHermes source tree (wiped on every Hermes update), the controller into\n`~/.hermes/scripts/`, and the skill into a category folder under\n`~/.hermes/skills/`. The three copies drifted, and each side found the\nothers by searching a hardcoded list of paths.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe package is published to npm. Its installer copies one directory into\nthe Hermes user plugin directory (`$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`).\nThat directory holds the routing backend, the controller and the skill. The\nrouting backend registers the skill itself through Hermes's plugin skill\nAPI, so nothing is written under `~/.hermes/skills/`. Every lookup between\nthe three is relative to that one directory.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **pip package.** Fits the runtime language, but Hermes runs in its own\n  Python environment and the controller runs on the system `python3`;\n  installing into the right interpreter is its own problem. npm gives a\n  zero-dependency `npx` installer that runs anywhere Node does.\n- **`hermes plugins install <git url>`.** Native, but it takes only git\n  URLs, gives us no hook to run `hermes config set`, and offers no\n  `doctor`.\n- **Separate skill copy under `~/.hermes/skills/`.** Editable by agents in\n  place, but that is exactly how the copies drifted before.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- npm delivers Python. Node is an install-time dependency only.\n- The installed copy is a snapshot: upgrading the package means running\n  `install` again.\n- The skill is read-only and namespaced (`tiiny-router:tiiny-model-routing`)\n  and disappears when the routing backend is disabled.\n- `uninstall` removes one directory.\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"route_check.py — show which Tiiny model a task goal would be routed to.\n\nA read-only companion to the routing backend. It applies the same tier table\nand the same shape detection, then prints the tier, the model, that model's\nNPU share and context window, and what the model's reasoning mode would be —\nso a routing decision can be checked without spawning a child agent.\n\nThe tier table comes from the plugin's ``tiers.py`` and the reasoning control\nfrom its ``thinking.py``: the same files the routing plugin reads, so this\nscript and the backend cannot drift apart. Both are located relative to this\nfile, because the plugin and the checker ship side by side in two layouts —\n``plugin/`` inside a skill, ``examples/tiiny-router/`` inside an article.\n\nUsage:\n    python3 route_check.py \"index every file under the vault and classify each\"\n    python3 route_check.py --tier code\n    python3 route_check.py --all          # every tier, with its budget\n    python3 route_check.py --image \"a photorealistic portrait\"\n    python3 route_check.py --thinking off \"summarise the meeting notes\"\n    python3 route_check.py --thinking on  \"solve this novel reasoning problem\"\n\nExit codes:\n    0  a route was found\n    1  the tier was not recognised\n    2  the usage was wrong\n\nThe script changes nothing on the device. It makes read-only calls: one to\nthe device's resident model list, and — only when a thinking mode is asked\nfor — one to the device's model catalogue, to read what that model can do\nwith reasoning.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport importlib.util\nimport os\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n#: Where the plugin's shared modules may live, relative to this script.\n_PLUGIN_DIRS = (\n    Path(\"plugin\"),\n    Path(\"examples\") / \"tiiny-router\",\n)\n\n\ndef _load(name: str, filename: str):\n    \"\"\"Load a shared plugin module by path, whichever layout it sits in.\"\"\"\n    here = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n    for candidate in _PLUGIN_DIRS:\n        path = here / candidate / filename\n        if not path.exists():\n            continue\n        spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(name, path)\n        if spec is None or spec.loader is None:\n            continue\n        module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n        spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n        return module\n    raise SystemExit(\n        f\"could not find {filename}. It ships next to the plugin: look in \"\n        + \", \".join(str(here / c) for c in _PLUGIN_DIRS)\n        + \".\"\n    )\n\n\ntiers = _load(\"tiiny_tiers\", \"tiers.py\")\nthinking = _load(\"tiiny_thinking\", \"thinking.py\")\nimport re\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\nimport urllib.error\nimport urllib.request\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# --- paths ------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nSKILL_ROOT = HERE.parent\nHERMES_HOME = Path(os.environ.get(\"HERMES_HOME\", \"~/.hermes\")).expanduser()\n\ntry:\n    import devices as D\nexcept Exception:\n    try:\n        import importlib.util\n        for cand in (HERE / \"devices.py\", HERMES_HOME / \"mesh\" / \"devices.py\"):\n            if cand.exists():\n                spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"devices\", cand)\n                if spec and spec.loader:\n                    D = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n                    spec.loader.exec_module(D)\n                    break\n        else:\n            D = None\n    except Exception:\n        D = None\n\n\ndef _shared_home() -> Path:\n    \"\"\"The BASE Hermes home, even when HERMES_HOME points at a profile.\n\n    Four files are shared state across every profile: the plan, the\n    cross-agent lock, the hold file, and the catalogue snapshot.\n\n    Two readers live in the base home and will not look anywhere else:\n\n    - the delegation plugin reads the plan from ``~/.hermes/tiiny-plan.json``\n    directory that has both ``hot.md`` and ``skills/`` in it.\n\n    Three ways to find it, in order: the ``TIINY_VAULT`` environment\n    variable, the same name in ``~/.hermes/.env``, and a walk up from this\n    file. The walk is what finds it for the master copy; the other two are\n    what an installed copy uses.\n\n    No machine path is hard-coded here. This file is published, and a\n    published file must not carry the path of the machine it was written on.\n    \"\"\"\n    override = os.environ.get(\"TIINY_VAULT\") or _dotenv_value(\"TIINY_VAULT\")\n    if override:\n        candidate = Path(override).expanduser()\n        return candidate if candidate.exists() else None\n    for base in (SKILL_ROOT, HERE):\n        for parent in (base, *base.parents):\n            try:\n                if (parent / \"hot.md\").exists() and (parent / \"skills\").exists():\n                    return parent\n            except OSError:\n                continue\n    return None\n\n\nVAULT = _find_vault()\n\n#: Shared state. These live in the BASE Hermes home, not the profile — see\n#: `_shared_home` for why, and for the failure that follows if they do not.\nSHARED_HOME = _shared_home()\n\n\n\n#: Default lock lifetime, in seconds. Long enough for a long research batch,\n#: short enough that a crashed agent does not lock the device overnight.\nDEFAULT_TTL = 1800\n\n\ndef _load_tiers():\n    \"\"\"Load the shared tier table by path (see tiers.py for why).\n\n    The table lives next to the plugin in the vault's skill directory, and\n    beside the installed plugin under the Hermes tree. Both are searched, so\n    the controller works from either copy of itself.\n\n    The published article repository lays the family out differently — the\n    plugin sits under ``skill/plugin`` and a copy under ``examples`` — so\n    those paths are searched too. Without them a reader who cloned the\n    repository and ran the published controller got \"could not find the tier\n    table\" on every command.\n    \"\"\"\n    import importlib.util\n\n    candidates = [\n        SKILL_ROOT / \"plugin\" / \"tiers.py\",\n        SKILL_ROOT / \"skill\" / \"plugin\" / \"tiers.py\",\n        SKILL_ROOT / \"examples\" / \"tiiny-router\" / \"tiers.py\",\n        HERE / \"tiers.py\",\n        Path(os.path.expanduser(\n            \"~/.hermes/hermes-agent/plugins/delegation/tiiny-router/tiers.py\")),\n    ]\n    path = next((c for c in candidates if c.exists()), None)\n    if path is None:\n        raise SystemExit(\n            \"could not find the tier table. Looked in: \"\n            + \", \".join(str(c) for c in candidates)\n        )\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"tiiny_tiers\", path)\n    if spec is None or spec.loader is None:\n        raise SystemExit(f\"could not load the tier table from {path}\")\n    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n    return module\n\n\ntiers = _load_tiers()\n\n\n#: what is not, with no loading.\n#:\n#: This is the config toggle for Stage 3.  The default is ``True`` — the\n#: ``ensure`` call makes the device ready for the child without an extra\n#: manual step.\nENSURE_ON_ROUTE = os.environ.get(\"TIINY_ENSURE_ON_ROUTE\", \"true\").lower() != \"false\"\n\n#: The controller module. Loaded by path (see ``tiers.py`` for why a\n#: relative import would break under the Hermes plugin loader).\n_CTL_SPEC = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\n    \"tiiny_controller\",\n    Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"scripts\" / \"tiiny_ctl.py\",\n)\nif _CTL_SPEC is None or _CTL_SPEC.loader is None:\n    ctl = None\nelse:\n    ctl = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_CTL_SPEC)\n    try:\n        _CTL_SPEC.loader.exec_module(ctl)\n    except Exception:\n        ctl = None\n\n\ndef device_key() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Return the device API key, or an empty string if it cannot be found.\n\nhermes-plugin-package/\nissues/\nlearnings.md\nprogress.md\nspec.md","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fa7ddb5-486f-4c1d-8d10-e98d3ec44829","uuid":"16386f2c-4d4d-4f8c-bb61-a3fb03b2005d","timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:41:34.924Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Ship as one Hermes user plugin directory, installed by npm\n\n**Status:** Accepted (2026-11-20)\n\n## Context\n\nThe routing backend, the controller and the skill are Python and Markdown\nthat run inside, or alongside, the Hermes harness. Before this decision they\nwere installed by hand into three places: the routing backend into the\nHermes source tree (wiped on every Hermes update), the controller into\n`~/.hermes/scripts/`, and the skill into a category folder under\n`~/.hermes/skills/`. The three copies drifted, and each side found the\nothers by searching a hardcoded list of paths.\n\n## Decision\n\nThe package is published to npm. Its installer copies one directory into\nthe Hermes user plugin directory (`$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`).\nThat directory holds the routing backend, the controller and the skill. The\nrouting backend registers the skill itself through Hermes's plugin skill\nAPI, so nothing is written under `~/.hermes/skills/`. Every lookup between\nthe three is relative to that one directory.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **pip package.** Fits the runtime language, but Hermes runs in its own\n  Python environment and the controller runs on the system `python3`;\n  installing into the right interpreter is its own problem. npm gives a\n  zero-dependency `npx` installer that runs anywhere Node does.\n- **`hermes plugins install <git url>`.** Native, but it takes only git\n  URLs, gives us no hook to run `hermes config set`, and offers no\n  `doctor`.\n- **Separate skill copy under `~/.hermes/skills/`.** Editable by agents in\n  place, but that is exactly how the copies drifted before.\n\n#