{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UhJjQmG4cB6nraMWbGrjQL","type":"tool_result","content":"tiiny-router:\n__init__.py\nplugin/\nplugin.yaml\nreferences/\nscripts/\nSKILL.md\ntemplates/\nthinking.py\ntiers.py\n\ntiiny-router/plugin:","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fa7ddb5-486f-4c1d-8d10-e98d3ec44829","uuid":"a3f2f2a7-5a47-4b7e-91bf-6af4c9deba43","timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:42:08.500Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"tiiny-router:\n__init__.py\nplugin/\nplugin.yaml\nreferences/\nscripts/\nSKILL.md\ntemplates/\nthinking.py\ntiers.py\n\ntiiny-router/plugin:","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/plugin/plugin.yaml","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":5,"newStart":0,"newLines":0,"lines":["-name: tiiny-router","-version: 2.1.0","-description: \"Delegation backend that routes each subtask to the Tiiny model matching its shape: research, index, code, browser, draft, general. Reads the device's resident set and the batch plan written by the lifecycle controller, so a specialist that was just loaded is the specialist the child gets. Never routes to a model that is not loaded, and never loads one itself. Also sets the reasoning mode per task - auto, on or off - from the device's own capability for the model it picked, and reports the state the model actually reached.\"","-author: Gary Garcia (garciacionet-alt), Hermes Agent","-kind: backend"]}],"deleted":true},{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/plugin/thinking.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":353,"newStart":0,"newLines":0,"lines":["-\"\"\"Reasoning-mode control for the Tiiny routing backend.","-","-The device publishes what each model can do with reasoning. It is read from","-the device **at route time** rather than kept in the tier table, because the","-Model Store changes with every TiinyOS update and a hand-maintained table","-goes stale quietly — a table that says a model reasons when it no longer does","-is worse than no table, because it is believed.","-","-Two endpoints carry the capability:","-","-``GET /v1/models``","-    Every model that is resident, with a ``thinking`` block. Small, and it is","-    the same read the router already makes for residency.","-","-``GET /api/v1/models/online_models``","-    Every model in the store, with the same ``thinking`` block. Large — the","-    entries carry full descriptions — so it is only read when a model that is","-    not resident has to be resolved.","-","-The block looks like this::","-","-    \"thinking\": {","-        \"supported\": true,            # the model can reason at all","-        \"toggleable\": true,           # a boolean on/off switch exists","-        \"levels\": [],                 # named reasoning levels, when it has any","-        \"enabled_by_default\": true,","-        \"default_level\": null,","-    }","-","-Two controls reach the device, and they are not interchangeable","-------------------------------------------------------------","-``extra_body.chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking``","-    A boolean, passed through the chat template. This is the decisive","-    control where the model honours it: the reasoning trace disappears and","-    the answer comes straight back.","-","-``reasoning_effort`` at the top level of the request","-    A named level, read by the inference server itself rather than by the","-    model's chat template. This is the control for a model whose chat","-    template has no boolean switch — and it is the *only* control for that","-    model, because the boolean is ignored outright.","-","-The same level name inside ``chat_template_kwargs`` is a **different** knob","-that only some chat templates read. Putting the level there works on one","-model family and is silently ignored by another, which is worse than not","-sending it: the route looks configured and the model does not change.","-","-The device's own ``toggleable`` flag is a **hint, not ground truth**. One","-model on this device is flagged non-toggleable and honours","-``enable_thinking: false`` perfectly well. So the boolean is sent whenever it","-can be sent, and the level is sent alongside it when the device says the","-boolean will not move this model. Which control actually took effect is","-reported in the route's label, so the operator sees the achieved state and","-not the requested one.","-","-What \"off\" means when the model cannot be turned off","-----------------------------------------------------","-Some models have no working switch. For those, \"off\" is not a refusal and","-not a pretence: it means **the cheapest state the model offers**. That is the","-lowest reasoning level it declares. The model still reasons — it just","-reasons less — and the label says so (``off→low``) rather than claiming a","-switch that does not exist.","-","-What this module will not do is guess. If the device does not report a","-model's capability, nothing is applied and the label says ``unknown``: the","-model's native behaviour is a known quantity, an invented one is not.","-","-Nothing here mutates the device. It reads, and it computes.","-\"\"\"","-","-from __future__ import annotations","-","-import json","-import os","-import time","-import urllib.request","-from typing import Any, Mapping","-","-#: The device's OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Local, on the LAN.","-TIINY_BASE_URL = os.environ.get(\"TIINY_BASE_URL\", \"http://openai.api.tiiny/v1\").rstrip(\"/\")","-","-#: The device's management host. Serves the full Model Store catalogue.","-TIINY_HOST = os.environ.get(\"TIINY_HOST\", \"http://tiinyhost.local\").rstrip(\"/\")","-","-#: Reasoning levels, cheapest first. Used only to pick the cheapest and the","-#: most expensive level out of the ones a model declares. A level the device","-#: does not name here still sorts — it just sorts after the named ones.","-LEVEL_ORDER = (\"none\", \"minimal\", \"low\", \"medium\", \"high\", \"xhigh\")","-","-#: The smallest output budget a reasoning model can finish inside.","-#:","-#: A reasoning model spends its budget on the trace first. With a small","-#: budget the request comes back HTTP 200 with an **empty** answer and the","-#: budget gone — a silent failure that looks like the model produced nothing.","-#: The floor is the budget children run with by default.","-THINKING_MAX_TOKENS = 4096","-","-#: How long a reasoning-capability lookup is reused, in seconds. The Model","-#: Store changes on a TiinyOS update, not on a heartbeat, so a long cache is","-#: safe and keeps the routing path cheap.","-CAPABILITY_TTL = 900","-","-#: Cached capability lookup for resident models: (timestamp, {id: capability}).","-_capability_cache: tuple[float, dict[str, dict[str, Any]]] | None = None","-","-#: Cached capability lookup for the whole store: (timestamp, {id: capability}).","-_catalogue_cache: tuple[float, dict[str, dict[str, Any]]] | None = None","-","-","-def device_key() -> str:","-    \"\"\"Return the device API key, or an empty string if it cannot be found.","-","-    Hermes keeps its secrets in ``~/.hermes/.env`` and resolves them through","-    its own accessor — they are **not** in the process environment. Reading","-    ``os.environ`` alone therefore finds nothing, and the router would","-    silently fail open on every call. Read it the way Hermes reads it, fall","-    back to the environment, and fall back to the dotenv file itself so the","-    standalone checker works outside Hermes.","-    \"\"\"","-    value = \"\"","-    try:","-        from hermes_cli.config import get_env_value_prefer_dotenv","-","-        value = get_env_value_prefer_dotenv(\"TIINY_API_KEY\") or \"\"","-    except Exception:","-        value = \"\"","-    value = (value or os.environ.get(\"TIINY_API_KEY\", \"\") or \"\").strip()","-    if value:","-        return value","-    try:","-        path = os.path.expanduser(\"~/.hermes/.env\")","-        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as handle:","-            for line in handle:","-                line = line.strip()","-                if line.startswith(\"TIINY_API_KEY\"):","-                    _, _, raw = line.partition(\"=\")","-                    return raw.strip().strip('\"').strip(\"'\")","-    except Exception:","-        pass","-    return \"\"","-","-","-def _read_json(url: str, key: str, timeout: float) -> Any:","-    request = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + key})","-    with urllib.request.urlopen(request, timeout=timeout) as response:","-        return json.load(response)","-","-","-def _entries(payload: Any) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:","-    \"\"\"Return the list of model entries in a catalogue response.\"\"\"","-    items = payload.get(\"data\") if isinstance(payload, dict) else payload","-    if isinstance(items, dict):","-        items = items.get(\"models\") or items.get(\"data\") or []","-    if not isinstance(items, list):","-        return []","-    return [entry for entry in items if isinstance(entry, dict)]","-","-","-def _capability_of(entry: Mapping[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:","-    \"\"\"Normalise one catalogue entry into a capability record.\"\"\"","-    thinking = entry.get(\"thinking\")","-    thinking = thinking if isinstance(thinking, Mapping) else {}","-    levels = thinking.get(\"levels\") or entry.get(\"reasoning_levels\") or []","-    if not isinstance(levels, list):","-        levels = []","-    return {","-        \"supported\": bool(thinking.get(\"supported\")),","-        \"toggleable\": bool(thinking.get(\"toggleable\")),","-        \"levels\": [str(level) for level in levels if isinstance(level, str)],","-        \"enabled_by_default\": bool(thinking.get(\"enabled_by_default\")),","-        \"default_level\": thinking.get(\"default_level\"),","-    }","-","-","-def _model_id(entry: Mapping[str, Any]) -> str:","-    for key in (\"model_id\", \"id\", \"fullname\", \"name\"):","-        value = entry.get(key)","-        if isinstance(value, str) and value:","-            return value","-    return \"\"","-","-","-def _resident_capabilities(refresh: bool = False) -> dict[str, dict[str, Any]]:","-    \"\"\"Return the capability of every resident model.\"\"\"","-    global _capability_cache","-    now = time.monotonic()","-    if not refresh and _capability_cache is not None:","-        if now - _capability_cache[0] < CAPABILITY_TTL:","-            return _capability_cache[1]","-","-    key = device_key()","-    caps: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}","-    if key:","-        try:","-            payload = _read_json(TIINY_BASE_URL + \"/models\", key, 3.0)","-            for entry in _entries(payload):","-                model_id = entry.get(\"id\") or _model_id(entry)","-                if isinstance(model_id, str) and model_id:","-                    caps[model_id] = _capability_of(entry)","-        except Exception:","-            caps = {}","-","-    _capability_cache = (now, caps)","-    return caps","-","-","-def _catalogue_capabilities(refresh: bool = False) -> dict[str, dict[str, Any]]:","-    \"\"\"Return the capability of every model in the store.","-","-    The catalogue entries carry full descriptions, so this is a heavy read.","-    It is only made when a model that is not resident has to be resolved, and","-    the answer is cached for ``CAPABILITY_TTL``.","-    \"\"\"","-    global _catalogue_cache","-    now = time.monotonic()","-    if not refresh and _catalogue_cache is not None:","-        if now - _catalogue_cache[0] < CAPABILITY_TTL:","-            return _catalogue_cache[1]","-","-    key = device_key()","-    caps: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] = {}","-    if key:","-        try:","-            payload = _read_json(TIINY_HOST + \"/api/v1/models/online_models\", key, 20.0)","-            for entry in _entries(payload):","-                model_id = _model_id(entry)","-                if model_id:","-                    caps.setdefault(model_id, _capability_of(entry))","-        except Exception:","-            caps = {}","-","-    _catalogue_cache = (now, caps)","-    return caps","-","-","-def thinking_capability(model: str) -> dict[str, Any] | None:","-    \"\"\"Return what the device says about a model's reasoning, or ``None``.","-","-    ``None`` means the device did not say — it was unreachable, or it does not","-    publish this model. The caller then applies nothing.","-    \"\"\"","-    if not model:","-        return None","-    capability = _resident_capabilities().get(model)","-    if capability is not None:","-        return capability","-    return _catalogue_capabilities().get(model)","-","-","-def _pick_level(levels: list[str], *, cheapest: bool) -> str | None:","-    \"\"\"Return the cheapest or the most expensive of a model's levels.\"\"\"","-    if not levels:","-        return None","-    ranked = sorted(","-        levels,","-        key=lambda level: (","-            LEVEL_ORDER.index(level) if level in LEVEL_ORDER else len(LEVEL_ORDER),","-            levels.index(level),","-        ),","-    )","-    return ranked[0] if cheapest else ranked[-1]","-","-","-def resolve_thinking(","-    model: str,","-    requested: str,","-    *,","-    max_tokens_floor: int = THINKING_MAX_TOKENS,","-) -> tuple[dict[str, Any] | None, str]:","-    \"\"\"Resolve a requested thinking mode against what the model can do.","-","-    Returns ``(request_overrides or None, achieved state)``.","-","-    The achieved state is what the route reports, and it is deliberately not","-    the requested one:","-","-    ``auto``","-        Nothing was applied. The model keeps its native behaviour.","-    ``on`` / ``off``","-        The boolean switch was applied and is the control.","-    ``on→high`` / ``off→low``","-        The model has no working boolean switch, so the named level was","-        applied instead — the most expensive one for ``on``, the cheapest for","-        ``off``. The model still reasons; it just reasons less.","-    ``unsupported``","-        The model does not reason at all, so ``on`` is not a thing that can","-        happen.","-    ``unknown``","-        The device did not report this model, so nothing was applied.","-    \"\"\"","-    requested = (requested or \"auto\").strip().lower()","-    if requested not in (\"auto\", \"on\", \"off\"):","-        raise ValueError(","-            f\"Unknown thinking mode {requested!r}. Valid modes are: auto, on, off.\"","-        )","-","-    if requested == \"auto\":","-        return None, \"auto\"","-","-    capability = thinking_capability(model)","-    if capability is None:","-        return None, \"unknown\"","-","-    if not capability[\"supported\"]:","-        # The model does not reason at all. \"on\" cannot happen; \"off\" is","-        # already the truth.","-        return None, (\"unsupported\" if requested == \"on\" else \"off\")","-","-    levels = capability[\"levels\"]","-    template_kwargs: dict[str, Any] = {\"enable_thinking\": requested == \"on\"}","-","-    overrides: dict[str, Any] = {","-        \"extra_body\": {\"chat_template_kwargs\": template_kwargs},","-    }","-","-    level: str | None = None","-    if levels and not capability[\"toggleable\"]:","-        # The device says the boolean cannot move this model, so the level is","-        # the control that works. It goes at the top level of the request,","-        # where the inference server reads it — inside","-        # ``chat_template_kwargs`` it would be ignored.","-        level = _pick_level(levels, cheapest=(requested == \"off\"))","-        if level:","-            overrides[\"reasoning_effort\"] = level","-","-    # The floor is needed whenever the model reasons at all — including in the","-    # \"off\" state, because a model whose boolean switch does not work still","-    # produces a trace.","-    if isinstance(max_tokens_floor, int) and max_tokens_floor > 0:","-        overrides[\"max_tokens\"] = max_tokens_floor","-","-    if level:","-        # The level is the effective control, so the label reports it.","-        achieved = f\"{requested}→{level}\"","-    else:","-        achieved = requested","-","-    return overrides, achieved","-","-","-def describe_capability(model: str) -> str:","-    \"\"\"Return a one-line description of a model's reasoning capability.\"\"\"","-    capability = thinking_capability(model)","-    if capability is None:","-        return \"unknown (the device did not report this model)\"","-    if not capability[\"supported\"]:","-        return \"no reasoning\"","-    levels = capability[\"levels\"]","-    if levels and not capability[\"toggleable\"]:","-        return f\"levels only ({', '.join(levels)}) — the on/off switch is ignored\"","-    if levels:","-        return f\"on/off switch, levels {', '.join(levels)}\"","-    return \"on/off switch\""]}],"deleted":true},{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/plugin/tiers.py","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":269,"newStart":0,"newLines":0,"lines":["-\"\"\"Shared tables for the Tiiny model-routing skill.","-","-One source of truth for the tier table, the shape signals, and the","-special-model table (image generation, OCR, music). Pure data and pure","-functions — no Hermes imports, no network calls, no device state — so the","-delegation plugin and the standalone scripts can both use it.","-","-**Why it is loaded by path and not by package name.** The Hermes plugin","-loader executes a plugin's ``__init__.py`` through","-``importlib.util.spec_from_file_location``, which does not establish package","-semantics: a relative ``from .tiers import ...`` fails there. And the scripts","-run outside Hermes entirely, where ``from agent...`` is not importable at all.","-Loading the file by path works in both places, so the table never forks.","-","-**The figures are the device's, read on 2026-11-01, re-verified 2026-11-03.** Every NPU share and","-context window below was read from ``GET /api/v1/models/online_models`` and","-checked against the live device. They go stale when TiinyOS updates the","-Model Store; ``scripts/tiiny_ctl.py catalog --refresh`` says so out loud","-rather than letting a stale number look authoritative.","-\"\"\"","-","-from __future__ import annotations","-","-#: The device's OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Local, on the LAN.","-TIINY_BASE_URL = \"http://openai.api.tiiny/v1\"","-","-#: The device's management host. Serves the Model Store catalogue.","-TIINY_HOST = \"http://tiinyhost.local\"","-","-#: Provider name as configured in ``providers:`` in config.yaml.","-TIINY_PROVIDER = \"custom:tiiny\"","-","-#: Task tier -> (model id, NPU share, context window).","-#:","-#: The NPU and context figures were read from the device's own catalogue","-#: endpoint. They are not decoration: the NPU share is what decides whether a","-#: model can stay resident alongside the others a batch needs, and the context","-#: window is the ceiling on how much a child can hold at once.","-#:","-#: A tier can list more than one candidate. The first is the default; the rest","-#: are the fallbacks in the order the device's own descriptions support.","-TIER_CHOICES: dict[str, tuple[tuple[str, int, int], ...]] = {","-    \"research\": (","-        (\"InternScience/Sage-A1.5-Turbo\", 48, 262144),","-        (\"endless-frontier/BigBang-v1-Turbo\", 54, 131072),","-    ),","-    \"index\": (","-        (\"openai/gpt-oss-20b\", 27, 131072),","-    ),","-    \"code\": (","-        (\"Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B\", 47, 262144),","-        (\"deepreinforce-ai/Ornith-1.0-35B\", 50, 131072),","-        (\"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct-Turbo\", 55, 65536),","-        (\"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next\", 94, 131072),","-    ),","-    \"browser\": (","-        (\"Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B\", 52, 262144),","-    ),","-    \"draft\": (","-        (\"Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B\", 29, 131072),","-    ),","-    \"general\": (","-        (\"Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B\", 47, 262144),","-    ),","-}","-","-#: Which model each tier resolves to — the first choice in its list.","-TIER_MODEL: dict[str, str] = {","-    tier: choices[0][0] for tier, choices in TIER_CHOICES.items()","-}","-","-#: The tier names a caller may pass explicitly.","-VALID_TIERS = tuple(sorted(TIER_MODEL))","-","-#: The generalist. Every tier falls back to it when nothing else is resident,","-#: because the generalist is what the watchdog keeps resident.","-GENERALIST = \"Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B\"","-","-#: Shape signals. These are matched against the task goal, lowercased.","-#:","-#: Ordering matters: the first tier with a signal wins, so the specific","-#: shapes are tested before the general ones.","-SHAPE_SIGNALS: tuple[tuple[str, tuple[str, ...]], ...] = (","-    (\"research\", (","-        \"research\", \"literature\", \"survey\", \"investigate\", \"find sources\",","-        \"web search\", \"search the web\", \"literature review\", \"deep dive\",","-        \"competitive analysis\", \"market analysis\", \"sweep the\",","-    )),","-    (\"index\", (","-        \"index\", \"indexing\", \"inventory\", \"classify\", \"classify every\",","-        \"categorize\", \"catalog\", \"catalogue\", \"list every file\", \"walk the\",","-        \"enumerate\", \"manifest\", \"tag every\", \"bulk\", \"batch classify\",","-    )),","-    (\"browser\", (","-        \"browser\", \"click through\", \"web ui\", \"web page\", \"fill in the form\",","-        \"navigate the site\", \"screenshot the\", \"scrape the page\", \"automate the browser\",","-    )),","-    (\"code\", (","-        \"code\", \"refactor\", \"implement\", \"write a function\", \"bug\", \"debug\",","-        \"fix the\", \"compile\", \"unit test\", \"patch the\", \"repository\", \"repo\",","-        \"module\", \"script that\", \"shell script\", \"migrate the schema\",","-    )),","-    (\"draft\", (","-        \"draft\", \"summar\", \"rewrite\", \"rephrase\", \"bullet\", \"outline\",","-        \"condense\", \"shorten\", \"proofread\", \"reword\", \"tl;dr\", \"summarise\",","-    )),","-)","-","-#: Models that do a job rather than hold a conversation. They are not","-#: delegation targets — a child speaks chat completions, and these do not —","-#: so they live in their own table, chosen by what the job IS rather than by","-#: the shape of a goal.","-#:","-#: id -> (NPU share, kind, role, when to reach for it)","-SPECIAL_MODELS: dict[str, tuple[int, str, str, str]] = {","-    # --- image generation ---","-    \"Tongyi-MAI/Z-Image-Turbo\": (","-        26, \"image\", \"default — photorealism and legible text\",","-        \"One image model that handles most things well. Also the one that \"","-        \"renders text accurately, so it is the pick for a logo, a title card \"","-        \"or any image with words in it. ~9s at 512x512, ~55s at 1024x1024.\",","-    ),","-    \"HiDream-ai/HiDream-O1-Image-Dev\": (","-        30, \"image\", \"maximum fidelity\",","-        \"The subject IS the detail — fur, foliage, reflections, complex \"","-        \"light. ~34s at 1024x1024, and it goes to 2048x2048. About 3x slower \"","-        \"than the default, so it earns its keep only when detail is the point.\",","-    ),","-    \"TaoBaiBai2025/Z-Image-Turbo-Creating-Realistic\": (","-        26, \"image\", \"realistic people\",","-        \"The subject is a person and what matters is skin, hair and fabric. \"","-        \"A LoRA on the Z-Image base, so it inherits its speed.\",","-    ),","-    \"YeiYeiArt/Z-Image-Turbo-CharacterDesignSheet\": (","-        26, \"image\", \"character design sheet\",","-        \"A character turnaround — several perspectives, facial expressions \"","-        \"and a colour palette in ONE image. A LoRA on the Z-Image base.\",","-    ),","-    \"fal/FLUX.2-klein-4B-Background-Remove\": (","-        26, \"image\", \"background removal — NOT a generator\",","-        \"You already HAVE a photo and want the subject cut out for product \"","-        \"photography or compositing. An adapter, so it runs in the same pass.\",","-    ),","-    # --- documents ---","-    \"PaddlePaddle/PP-OCRv6-Medium\": (","-        1, \"ocr\", \"text extraction from images\",","-        \"Reading text out of a scanned page, a screenshot or a photo. 1% NPU, \"","-        \"so it costs almost nothing to keep around.\",","-    ),","-    \"PaddlePaddle/PP-DocLayoutV3\": (","-        20, \"ocr\", \"document layout analysis\",","-        \"Where the blocks are on a page — tables, columns, figures. The \"","-        \"companion to the OCR model, not a replacement for it.\",","-    ),","-    # --- audio ---","-    \"tencent/SongGeneration-v2-large\": (","-        28, \"music\", \"music generation\",","-        \"A song from a description: vocals, structure, instrumentation.\",","-    ),","-    \"RoyalCities/Foundation-1\": (","-        5, \"music\", \"short instrumental clips\",","-        \"A quick instrumental bed — a sting, a loop, a background cue. 5% NPU.\",","-    ),","-}","-","-#: The default model per special kind, used when no cue matches.","-SPECIAL_DEFAULTS: dict[str, str] = {","-    \"image\": \"Tongyi-MAI/Z-Image-Turbo\",","-    \"ocr\": \"PaddlePaddle/PP-OCRv6-Medium\",","-    \"music\": \"tencent/SongGeneration-v2-large\",","-}","-","-#: Cue -> model. Ordered from most specific to least; the first kind whose","-#: cue matches wins, so a request that says \"photorealistic logo\" gets the","-#: text-accurate default rather than the high-fidelity model.","-SPECIAL_CUES: tuple[tuple[str, tuple[str, ...], str], ...] = (","-    (\"image\", (","-        \"character sheet\", \"turnaround\", \"character design\", \"expression sheet\",","-    ), \"YeiYeiArt/Z-Image-Turbo-CharacterDesignSheet\"),","-    (\"image\", (","-        \"cut out\", \"cutout\", \"remove the background\", \"background removal\",","-        \"isolate the subject\", \"composite\",","-    ), \"fal/FLUX.2-klein-4B-Background-Remove\"),","-    (\"image\", (","-        \"maximum fidelity\", \"highest fidelity\", \"ultra detailed\", \"fine detail\",","-        \"complex lighting\", \"reflections\", \"foliage\", \"fur\",","-        \"2048\", \"4k\",","-    ), \"HiDream-ai/HiDream-O1-Image-Dev\"),","-    (\"image\", (","-        \"realistic person\", \"realistic people\", \"portrait of a man\",","-        \"portrait of a woman\", \"realistic human\", \"skin texture\",","-    ), \"TaoBaiBai2025/Z-Image-Turbo-Creating-Realistic\"),","-)","-","-#: Sizes verified to work on this device. Anything else is a guess, and the","-#: device's error is precise about why.","-KNOWN_GOOD_SIZES: dict[str, tuple[str, ...]] = {","-    \"Tongyi-MAI/Z-Image-Turbo\": (\"1024x1024\", \"1280x768\", \"1152x768\", \"1024x768\", \"512x512\"),","-    \"HiDream-ai/HiDream-O1-Image-Dev\": (\"1024x1024\", \"2048x2048\", \"1536x1024\", \"1024x1536\"),","-}","-","-","-def detect_tier(goal: str) -> str:","-    \"\"\"Return the task tier for a goal, or ``general`` when unrecognised.","-","-    The shape is read from the goal text because shape is what predicts which","-    model does well. A goal that mentions \"index the vault\" is an indexing","-    job; a goal that says \"refactor these three modules\" is a coding job.","-    Matching on the *subject* is brittle in a different way: a research task","-    about code matches code keywords and gets the coder.","-    \"\"\"","-    text = (goal or \"\").lower()","-    for tier, signals in SHAPE_SIGNALS:","-        for signal in signals:","-            if signal in text:","-                return tier","-    return \"general\"","-","-","-def tier_cost(tier: str) -> tuple[int, int]:","-    \"\"\"Return the (NPU share, context window) of a tier's default model.\"\"\"","-    model, npu, ctx = TIER_CHOICES[tier][0]","-    return npu, ctx","-","-","-def model_npu(model: str) -> int | None:","-    \"\"\"Return the NPU share of a model, from whichever table has it.\"\"\"","-    for choices in TIER_CHOICES.values():","-        for name, npu, _ctx in choices:","-            if name == model:","-                return npu","-    entry = SPECIAL_MODELS.get(model)","-    if entry:","-        return entry[0]","-    return None","-","-","-def model_context(model: str) -> int | None:","-    \"\"\"Return the context window of a model, from whichever table has it.\"\"\"","-    for choices in TIER_CHOICES.values():","-        for name, _npu, ctx in choices:","-            if name == model:","-                return ctx","-    return None","-","-","-def pick_special_model(description: str, kind: str = \"image\") -> tuple[str, str]:","-    \"\"\"Choose a special model for a job description.","-","-    Returns ``(model id, reason)``. The reason is what makes the choice","-    arguable rather than magic: it names the cue that matched, or says the","-    default was used because nothing more specific did.","-","-    A cue only wins if its model is one this device can actually run. The","-    candidate list is the table's entries for that kind; the *availability*","-    check happens against the device's download state, which the caller","-    supplies.","-    \"\"\"","-    text = (description or \"\").lower()","-    for cue_kind, cues, model in SPECIAL_CUES:","-        if cue_kind != kind:","-            continue","-        for cue in cues:","-            if cue in text:","-                return model, f\"matched '{cue}'\"","-    default = SPECIAL_DEFAULTS.get(kind)","-    if default is None:","-        raise KeyError(f\"no default special model for kind {kind!r}\")","-    return default, \"default — nothing more specific matched\""]}],"deleted":true},{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/references/backend.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":260,"newStart":0,"newLines":0,"lines":["-# The routing backend","-","-The delegation backend that routes each subtask to the model that matches its","-shape. Install it, then select it in the active profile's config.","-","-## What it does","-","-Core calls `route_task(task, config)` once per delegated subtask. The","-backend inspects that subtask's goal, picks a tier, and returns the model,","-provider, endpoint, and request overrides for that subtask alone.","-","-Without it, `delegation.model` pins one model for every child in the batch.","-","-**It chooses; it never loads.** The device's resident set is a shared, finite","-resource and a load is a swap that evicts whatever was resident, so the","-loading half of the job lives in `scripts/tiiny_ctl.py` — a step the manager","-agent takes explicitly. See [lifecycle.md](lifecycle.md).","-","-The two halves meet at the **plan** (`~/.hermes/tiiny-plan.json`): the","-controller writes it when it plans a batch, and the router reads it when it","-routes each subtask. That is how a specialist the controller just loaded","-becomes the specialist the child actually runs on.","-","-## Install","-","-1. Copy the plugin directory into your Hermes plugins tree. **All three files","-   matter** — `tiers.py` holds the table the plugin and the scripts share, and","-   `thinking.py` holds the reasoning-mode control:","-","-   ```bash","-   cp -r plugin ~/.hermes/hermes-agent/plugins/delegation/tiiny-router/","-   ```","-","-2. Add the device as a provider in the active profile's `config.yaml`:","-","-   ```yaml","-   providers:","-     tiiny:","-       name: tiiny","-       api: http://openai.api.tiiny/v1","-       key_env: TIINY_API_KEY","-       transport: chat_completions","-       default_model: Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B","-       context_length: 262144","-       extra_body:","-         chat_template_kwargs:","-           enable_thinking: false","-       models:","-         Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B: {context_length: 262144}","-         Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B: {context_length: 262144}","-         Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B: {context_length: 131072}","-         openai/gpt-oss-20b: {context_length: 131072}","-         deepreinforce-ai/Ornith-1.0-35B: {context_length: 131072}","-         InternScience/Sage-A1.5-Turbo: {context_length: 262144}","-   ```","-","-   The bearer goes in the environment as `TIINY_API_KEY`.","-","-   `models_discovered: false` matters: with it on, a live probe can wipe the","-   metadata above and leave a model with the wrong context length.","-","-3. Select the backend in the same `config.yaml`:","-","-   ```yaml","-   delegation:","-     backend: tiiny-router","-     fallback_providers:","-       - provider: minimax","-         model: MiniMax-M3","-   ```","-","-   The fallback matters: if the device is unreachable, the batch should still","-   complete on a paid provider rather than fail. It should also be visible","-   when it happens — a silent fallback means the local tier is not actually","-   being used.","-","-4. Restart the agent so the plugin and the new schema are picked up. If the","-   agent runs under a gateway that cannot be restarted, the gateway's","-   control socket reloads plugins in place:","-","-   ```python","-   from pathlib import Path","-   from gateway.control_socket import reload_gateway_plugins","-   from hermes_constants import get_hermes_home","-","-   reload_gateway_plugins(Path(get_hermes_home()))","-   ```","-","-## Verify","-","-```bash","-python3 ../scripts/route_check.py \"index every file under the vault and classify each\"","-python3 ../scripts/route_check.py --thinking off \"index every file under the vault\"","-python3 ../scripts/tiiny_ctl.py status","-```","-","-The checker prints the tier, the model, that model's NPU share and context","-window, what the model can do with reasoning, and whether it is currently","-resident. The controller prints the device, the resident set, the lock, the","-hold and the plan.","-","-To confirm the backend is live, delegate a batch with mixed subtasks and read","-the `route` on each child's result — it carries the backend name and the","-tier label, with the achieved reasoning state on it.","-","-## Thinking mode","-","-Each task may carry `thinking: \"auto\" | \"on\" | \"off\"`. The default is","-`auto`, which changes nothing and leaves the model's native behaviour alone.","-","-The router reads the device's own capability for the model it picked, and","-applies the control that model actually honours. Two knobs exist and they","-are not interchangeable:","-","-| Control | Where it goes | Who honours it |","-|---|---|---|","-| `enable_thinking` | `extra_body.chat_template_kwargs` | Models whose chat template has the switch |","-| `reasoning_effort` | Top level of the request | The inference server, for models whose chat template has no switch |","-","-A level placed inside `chat_template_kwargs` is a **different** knob: some","-chat templates read it, others ignore it silently. Put the level at the top","-level of the request.","-","-Where a model has no working switch, `off` means **its cheapest reasoning","-level**, not a refusal. The model still reasons; it just reasons less.","-","-The route's label carries the achieved state, never the requested one:","-","-```","-index [think:off→low]","-index [think:off]","-general [think:unsupported]","-```","-","-A reasoning model also needs an output floor. With a small `max_tokens` the","-trace eats the budget and the request comes back HTTP 200 with an empty","-answer. The router applies a floor of 4096; raise it with","-`delegation.backends.tiiny-router.thinking_max_tokens` if you raise your own","-budget.","-","-## The tiers","-","-| Tier | Model | NPU | Context | Reasoning |","-|---|---|---|---|---|","-| `research` | `InternScience/Sage-A1.5-Turbo` | 48% | 262144 | switch |","-| `research` (alt) | `endless-frontier/BigBang-v1-Turbo` | 54% | 131072 | switch |","-| `index` | `openai/gpt-oss-20b` | 27% | 131072 | levels only |","-| `code` | `Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct-Turbo` | 55% | 65536 | none |","-| `code` (alt) | `deepreinforce-ai/Ornith-1.0-35B` | 50% | 131072 | switch |","-| `code` (alt) | `Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B` | 47% | 262144 | switch |","-| `code` (heavy) | `Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next` | 94% | 131072 | none |","-| `browser` | `Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B` | 52% | 262144 | switch |","-| `draft` | `Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B` | 29% | 131072 | switch |","-| `general` | `Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B` | 47% | 262144 | switch |","-","-**Re-read these numbers before trusting them.** They came from one device's","-catalogue endpoint on 2026-11-09, when the store held 92 models. The store","-changes with every TiinyOS update, and the NPU shares have already moved","-once.","-","-The reasoning column is the same kind of snapshot, and the device is the","-authority on it: the router reads the capability at route time, so a stale","-row here cannot break a route.","-","-They live in **`plugin/tiers.py`**, which is the single source of truth: the","-plugin, the controller and the checker all read that one file, so they cannot","-drift apart. It is loaded by path rather than by package name, because the","-Hermes plugin loader executes `__init__.py` through `spec_from_file_location`","-— which does not establish package semantics, so a relative import would","-fail there. `plugin/thinking.py` is loaded the same way, and is kept free of","-Hermes imports so the standalone checker can use it too.","-","-## Changing a tier","-","-Three edits, in this order, all in `plugin/tiers.py`:","-","-1. `TIER_CHOICES` — the model id, its NPU share, and its context window. All","-   three come from the device; `tiiny_ctl.py catalog --refresh` tells you","-   when they have moved.","-2. `TIER_MODEL` — derived from `TIER_CHOICES`; it needs no separate edit","-   unless a tier's default changes.","-3. `SHAPE_SIGNALS` — the signals that route a task to that tier. More","-   specific shapes come first; the first tier with a matching signal wins.","-","-Then update the same table in `SKILL.md`, and re-run the checker on a known","-goal.","-","-## Things that will bite","-","-- **The route's shape is the credential path.** The backend returns the","-  delegation section's own shape with only the model overridden — the way","-  the default backend returns `dict(config)`. This is not cosmetic. A route","-  with `base_url` set and `api_key` empty is a *direct endpoint*, and an","-  empty key means **inherit the parent's key**. The parent runs on the paid","-  provider, so the device would receive the wrong bearer and answer","-  `401 auth_failed` — and the child would fall back to the paid provider,","-  invisibly. Returning the section's shape puts this backend on the","-  provider-resolution branch, where the device's `key_env` is honoured.","-- **The router reads residency, and that changes the route.** It queries","-  `GET /v1/models` on the inference endpoint (30-second cache) and picks a","-  model that is actually loaded: the plan's assignment if there is one, then","-  the tier's first choice, then another candidate from the same tier, then","-  the generalist. A model that is not resident answers `404 \"is not loaded\"`,","-  which Hermes treats as terminal and falls back to the paid provider — so","-  routing to an unloaded model silently moves work off the device. The","-  route's `label` records any substitution (`code->generalist`). If the","-  lookup fails, the router fails open to the tier's first choice.","-- **The router never loads a model.** A load is a swap, and it evicts","-  whatever was resident — including the model a sibling task is using. The","-  controller does the loading, explicitly, under a lock.","-- **An unknown tier is refused.** The override fails loudly rather than","-  falling back to the generalist, because a silent fallback is invisible in","-  the output and expensive in the tokens.","-- **The task schema is cached.** `task_parameters()` and `description()` must","-  be deterministic for a given config — the schema is part of the cached","-  prompt prefix, so a non-deterministic result changes the prompt between","-  calls.","-- **Thinking mode is per task, not per config.** `thinking: \"auto\" | \"on\" |","-  \"off\"` is a task parameter, and the route's label reports the state the","-  model actually reached. Do not read \"off\" in the request as \"off\" in the","-  model: a model with no switch ends up at its cheapest level instead, and","-  the label says `off→low`.","-- **Two reasoning knobs, and they go in different places.**","-  `enable_thinking` belongs in `extra_body.chat_template_kwargs`; a named","-  level belongs at the **top level of the request**, not inside","-  `chat_template_kwargs`. The same level name inside the chat template is a","-  different knob that some model families read and others ignore silently —","-  which looks configured and changes nothing.","-- **The device's `toggleable` flag has been wrong.** A model flagged as","-  having no on/off switch honours it anyway. Send the boolean whenever it","-  can be sent, and let the label report what actually took effect.","-- **A reasoning model with a small `max_tokens` returns an empty response**","-  with the budget spent in the trace, and the status code is 200. The router","-  applies an output floor for this reason.","-- **Hermes secrets are not in the environment.** The device key lives in","-  `~/.hermes/.env` and is read through `hermes_cli.config`'s accessor. A","-  plugin that reads `os.environ` finds nothing, and the residency check","-  fails open on every call.","-- **A partially-installed plugin fails at load, not at use.** The plugin","-  loader executes `__init__.py` through `spec_from_file_location`, so","-  `__init__.py` cannot use a relative import to reach `tiers.py` — it loads","-  that file by path. Copy the whole `plugin/` directory, not just","-  `__init__.py` and `plugin.yaml`. A tree with `__init__.py` but no","-  `tiers.py` raises `ImportError` at load, and the backend is then simply","-  absent from `hermes plugins list` — which reads as \"never installed\"","-  rather than \"installed wrong\". Validate with","-  `hermes plugins validate <dir>`. The same applies to `thinking.py`.","-- **The installed skill and the vault skill drift apart.** The vault copy","-  under `skills/tiiny-model-routing/` is the source of truth; the installed","-  copies live under `~/.hermes/skills/tiiny-model-routing/` and","-  `~/.hermes/skills/mlops/tiiny-model-routing/`. A stale installed copy ends","-  up carrying its own literal copy of the tier table instead of importing","-  `plugin/tiers.py`, and the table starts drifting. Diff all three before","-  trusting any of them, and re-sync vault → installed after any table change.","-- **A saved `delegation.backend` does not change a running chat.** The","-  `delegate_task` schema is cached in the prompt prefix, so a config edit","-  applies from the next session (`/new`), not the current one. Verify the","-  backend in a fresh process rather than expecting the current session to","-  re-route:","-  `python3 -c \"from agent import delegation_backends as db; print(db.list_backends())\"`"]}],"deleted":true},{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/references/coding-delegation.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":329,"newStart":0,"newLines":0,"lines":["-# Delegating coding work to a Tiiny","-","-**The appliance writes the code. The manager agent judges it.** A paid","-frontier model in the main loop is for judgement, conversation and","-decisions; the token-heavy work belongs on the box on the LAN, where it","-costs nothing.","-","-A 30B model on an appliance is not a frontier model. The difference is not","-capability — it is **briefing**. Give it a tight, verifiable order and it","-competes. Give it a vague one and it wanders, and the manager pays for","-the wandering twice: once in the box's tokens, once in a re-dispatch.","-","----","-","-## 0. The shape","-","-```","-   ORDER ──▶ DISPATCH ──▶ OBSERVE ──▶ ┌──▶ ACCEPT","-     ▲                                 │","-     └──── CORRECT ◀───────────────────┘","-```","-","-| step | who | cost |","-|---|---|---|","-| Order | manager | paid, small |","-| Dispatch | manager | free |","-| Observe | manager | paid, small |","-| Correct | manager | paid, small |","-| Read, edit, test, document | appliance | free |","-","----","-","-## 1. Preflight — the gate","-","-Nothing is dispatched until this passes.","-","-```bash","-cd ~/.hermes/skills/mlops/tiiny-model-routing","-python3 scripts/route_check.py --thinking off \"<the goal>\"","-```","-","-Read the **residency** line, not the tier line.","-","-| residency | what to do |","-|---|---|","-| `loaded` | dispatch it |","-| `NOT loaded` | do **not** force that tier — either load the model first, or drop the override and take the resident model |","-","-**A forced tier overrides residency.** `delegate_task(tier=...)` selects","-the tier's first choice and sends it, without checking what is loaded. A","-model that is not resident answers 404; Hermes treats 404 as terminal; the","-child falls back to the paid provider *invisibly*, with a good answer and","-a bill. The tier is a hint; residency is the constraint.","-","-Preflight is cheap. A silent fallback is not.","-","----","-","-## 2. Box assignment","-","-| | provider | role |","-|---|---|---|","-| Box A | the one `TIINY_BASE_URL` points at | primary worker — the residency probe reads this box, so this is the box a tier must be resident on |","-| Box B | the other, by its own address and bearer | second worker |","-","-**One heavy child per box.** The NPU is one pool per appliance and each","-box serves one generation-heavy stream. Two children on one box starve","-each other, and the failure mode is a *hang*, not an error — the device","-keeps reporting healthy while it answers nothing. Two boxes give two","-genuinely parallel free streams.","-","-**A load is a swap.** It evicts whatever was resident, including the","-generalist the next wave will want. Load deliberately, and restore","-deliberately.","-","-### Make the box match the router, not the router match the box","-","-When you want a specialist and the router probes Box A, put the","-specialist on **Box A**. Do not repoint `TIINY_BASE_URL`, and do not wait","-for a restart.","-","-`TIINY_BASE_URL` is read from the environment when the plugin is","-imported, so changing it only takes effect in a new process. That makes","-\"the specialist is downloaded on Box B\" look like a blocked path. It is","-not. A model that is merely *downloaded* on Box A costs nothing to load,","-and once it is resident there `route_check.py` reports `loaded` and the","-tier routes to it with no config change at all.","-","-Measured: downloading a 55% specialist took about 20 minutes (free, in","-the background, while other work continued); loading it afterwards took","-20 seconds. The download is the slow part and it is unattended — start it","-early, keep working, and switch the tier when it lands.","-","-### Each box has its own bearer, and the wrong one looks like a dead box","-","-```","-TIINY_API_KEY     -> Box A","-TIINY_API_KEY_2   -> Box B","-```","-","-Point the controller at Box B without swapping the bearer and it answers","-`HTTP 401 {\"error\":\"auth_failed\"}`, which the controller reports as","-`device UNREACHABLE`. **That is a wrong key, not a down box**, and the","-wrong conclusion from it is \"the second box cannot be used\". Confirm with","-a one-line `curl` to that box's `/v1/models` using its own bearer before","-saying anything about reachability.","-","-Each box also needs its own lock, hold and plan files, or two agents","-fight over one lock:","-","-```bash","-set -a; . ~/.hermes/.env; set +a","-cd ~/.hermes/skills/mlops/tiiny-model-routing","-TIINY_API_KEY=\"$TIINY_API_KEY_2\" \\","-TIINY_DEVICE_ADDRESS=192.0.2.11 \\","-TIINY_BASE_URL=http://192.0.2.11/v1 \\","-TIINY_HOST=http://192.0.2.11 \\","-TIINY_LOCK_FILE=$HOME/.hermes/tiiny-lock-b.json \\","-TIINY_HOLD_FILE=$HOME/.hermes/tiiny-hold-b.json \\","-TIINY_PLAN_FILE=$HOME/.hermes/tiiny-plan-b.json \\","-python3 scripts/tiiny_ctl.py status","-```","-","-The mesh is the simpler door for both boxes when one is in front of them:","-`POST /mesh/lifecycle` with `action: start|stop|download` and a `target`.","-","----","-","-## 3. The work order","-","-Copy [../templates/work-order.md](../templates/work-order.md) and fill it","-in. Every order carries:","-","-- **one job, one file.** No multi-file refactors in a single order.","-- **exact absolute paths.** Never a relative path the child has to guess.","-- **exact anchors.** The function to change, the literal string to match","-  — quote it. \"Update the routing section\" is not an anchor.","-- **a runnable acceptance command.** The child must make it pass, and the","-  manager runs it again independently.","-- **the output artifact path.**","-- **no `<...>` placeholders.** The delegation backend refuses a goal","-  containing an unexpanded template marker. Write the literal expected","-  value.","-- **a self-check before reporting.** The child runs the acceptance","-  command itself and quotes the output.","-- **for anything risky: write to scratch, then move into place.**","-- **name the paths the child must NOT touch, and say what \"shipped\" means.**","-  A child asked to \"update the builder\" will find a convenient artifact to","-  run it against. If a build script writes into the live tree, the child will","-  rebuild a **shipped** artifact: one that already went out, already carried","-  hand-written content, and already had its own publication state recorded.","-  The rebuild succeeds, reports clean, and silently replaces authored work","-  with a generated blank. Write the exclusion into the order — *\"edit ONLY","-  `<file>`; do not run the builder against `<live path>`\"* — and prefer a","-  builder that refuses to overwrite an existing output directory.","-- **A generated placeholder is a trap when the output already has human","-  content.** If the generator writes an empty marked placeholder (an analysis","-  section, a body copy, a filled-in checklist), then re-running it over","-  anything a human has written into **deletes that content**, and the","-  placeholder looks correct. Check what the generator writes before pointing","-  it at anything that has shipped.","-- **keep prompt context under 10K tokens.** Never paste a multi-wave project","-  plan or multiple large reference files into a child brief. An appliance model","-  with a 64K context window (like `Qwen3-Coder-30B`) experiences hardware PCIe DMA","-  timeouts (`pcie_hdma_timeout`) when context approaches ~40K tokens, hanging the","-  socket indefinitely without returning an error. For repo-scale multi-file","-  tasks, route to a 256K context model (`Qwen3.6-35B-A3B`) or split the work into","-  single-file orders.","-- **proven worker recipe: Qwen3.6-35B-A3B with thinking off.** When delegating","-  implementation (e.g., a standalone module + unit test suite), route to","-  `Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B` on TinyAnt with `thinking: \"off\"`. Provide an explicit","-  interface specification, input/output schemas, and a runnable acceptance","-  command (`python3 test_X.py`). This avoids reasoning trace token burn, stays well","-  within context limits, and reliably produces clean, 100% passing suites (e.g., 9/9","-  passing tests) in one shot.","-","-Ask for raw findings on disk early and keep the summary short. That is","-what keeps a local model competitive with a frontier one — and it means a","-budget-exhausted child still leaves you its artifact rather than nothing.","-","-**Tell it to write the file before it verifies it.** An appliance","-generates at roughly 20 tokens per second, so a 150-line script is minutes","-of pure generation. A child that composes perfectly and never writes","-loses everything if it stalls. A slightly imperfect file on disk that the","-manager can fix beats a perfect one that never lands — say so in the","-order itself.","-","-That throughput is the real constraint on order size, not the model's","-competence. Budget an order in minutes: one file, a few hundred lines at","-most, one acceptance command. Every extra feature costs real wall-clock","-time on a box.","-","----","-","-## 4. Observe","-","-- **A child's report is a self-report. The artifact is the evidence.**","-","-- Read the **diff**, not the summary.","-- **Run the acceptance command yourself.** A child that says the tests","-  pass has not run your tests.","-- **A child that verifies by string-matching has not verified.** A sweep","-  that rewrites paths will report \"N references rewritten, all resolve\"","-  after checking that each new path *string* is present in the file — which","-  passes even when the path does not resolve from that file's own","-  directory. Make the acceptance check **resolve the path**: join it","-  against the directory of the file that holds it and assert the target","-  exists. A relative path is only correct relative to something, and","-  `../` depth is the thing a rewrite gets wrong: a file two levels below","-  the root needs `../../`, and both `../` and `../../../` look plausible","-  in the source.","-- **A rewrite that changes what a sentence says is a corruption, not a","-  fix.** Path tokens appear inside prose that *describes* a path — \"the","-  design system links to `../brand/tap-monogram.png`\" — and rewriting","-  that mention to a vault-absolute path breaks the sentence's claim","-  while looking like a repair. After a bulk rewrite, read the changed","-  lines in context: a mention inside a description keeps its original","-  form, and only a genuine link target gets rebased.","-- **Exercise every branch, especially the ones the report does not","-  mention.** A child that verifies `status` and `preflight` and reports","-  \"acceptance passed\" has told you nothing about `load` and `release`.","-  Invoke each subcommand once. An argument-forwarding bug (`$1` where","-  `$2` was meant) survives a green report and only shows itself when the","-  branch actually runs.","-- **A redacted secret looks like a hardcoded one.** Tool output can show","-  `Bearer ***` where the file actually reads `Bearer $(_key)`. Check by","-  length, or grep for the literal value, before raising a leak alarm —","-  that is the tool protecting the secret, not the child leaking it.","-- Read the **route label**. `tiiny-router` means the box served it.","-  Anything else means the paid provider did the work.","-- If the child ran long, look for its file on disk before concluding it","-  produced nothing — the hang is often in the handover, not the work.","-- **Record what you corrected, in the child's own report file.** When the","-  child's work needed fixing, the report it left behind still claims the","-  pre-fix state, so the next reader inherits a false record. Add the","-  corrections to the report as a verification block naming each defect,","-  what it was, and how it was resolved — and state plainly whether the","-  child's count and its self-check were accurate.","-- **After a child runs a build, check what the build TOUCHED, not only what","-  it was asked to change.** A child's report lists the files it meant to","-  edit; it does not list the artifacts its build wrote. Compare the","-  modification times of everything the build could have reached, or hash","-  the shipped files before and after. A shipped file that changed without","-  appearing in the report was clobbered — and if it held authored content,","-  the recovery path is whatever copy exists outside the tree (a scratch","-  build directory, a version-control copy, the platform's own read-back),","-  so **keep that copy before dispatching the child**.","-","----","-","-## 5. Correct","-","-A failing order gets a **second** order carrying the diff and the failure","-output as evidence. Never a re-brief of the original: a re-brief pays for","-the same mistake twice and gives the child no new information.","-","-```","-The change you made to <file> does this:","-<the diff>","-","-Running <the acceptance command> produces:","-<the output>","-","-Fix that, and change nothing else.","-```","-","----","-","-## 6. Release","-","-After every wave: stop the specialist, restore the required set, clear","-the lock and the hold. A swap that is not restored breaks every later","-order, and it looks like a model problem rather than a leftover state.","-","----","-","-## 7. The fallback alarm","-","-Three guards, strongest first:","-","-1. **Preflight** — makes it nearly impossible.","-2. **The route label** — read it every wave.","-3. **A ledger** — count the children whose route is not `tiiny-router`.","-   That count *is* the paid spend, and it should be zero.","-","----","-","-## 8. What to keep and what to give away","-","-| Keep (paid, small) | Give away (free, large) |","-|---|---|","-| writing the order | reading and editing the files |","-| reading the diff | running the tests |","-| judging it against the spec | test scaffolding and boilerplate |","-| choosing the architecture | bulk mechanical edits |","-| the final acceptance call | docs, docstrings, refactors, repro scripts |","-","-Target: **more than 80% of delegated tokens on an appliance.**","-","----","-","-## 9. During a delegated run, stop the auto-loader","-","-A gateway that puts the appliances back to their default models at startup","-will evict the specialist you just loaded, mid-batch. The TiinyMesh","-gateway has an `auto_restore` flag for exactly this — see the","-`tiiny-mesh-multi-target` skill.","-","----","-","-## 10. Rules, short","-","-1. **The manager does not write the code.** Reaching for `patch` or","-   `write_file` on the target file is the expensive model doing the","-   worker's job — the exact inversion this discipline exists to prevent.","-   Write the order, read the diff, run the acceptance, decide. The single","-   exception is a correction you can make in one edit (a wrong variable","-   reference) where a delegation round trip would cost more than the fix;","-   make it, and say plainly that you did.","-2. **Never force a tier whose model is not resident.** Check with","-   `route_check.py` first.","-3. **One heavy child per box.** Two boxes, two streams.","-4. **One job per order.** One file. Exact anchors. A runnable acceptance","-   command.","-5. **A child's summary is not evidence.** Run the acceptance command","-   yourself, and invoke every branch.","-6. **Correct with a diff, not a re-brief.**","-7. **Release after every wave.**","-8. **Watch the route label.** It is the invoice."]}],"deleted":true}],"moreFiles":29,"changedFiles":["/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/SKILL.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/plugin/__init__.py","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/plugin/plugin.yaml","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/plugin/thinking.py","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/plugin/tiers.py","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/references/backend.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/references/coding-delegation.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/references/image-models.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/references/lifecycle.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/references/project-role-selection.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/references/single-source-deployment.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/references/two-box-capability-matrix.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/scripts/route_check.py","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/scripts/tiiny-swap.sh","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/scripts/tiiny_ctl.py","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/scripts/tiiny_two_box_matrix.py","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/skill/templates/work-order.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/SKILL.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/__init__.py","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/plugin.yaml","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/references/backend.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/references/coding-delegation.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/references/image-models.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/references/lifecycle.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/references/project-role-selection.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/references/single-source-deployment.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/references/two-box-capability-matrix.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/scripts/route_check.py","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/scripts/tiiny-swap.sh","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/scripts/tiiny_ctl.py","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/scripts/tiiny_two_box_matrix.py","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/templates/work-order.md","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/thinking.py","/Users/nick/code/tiiny_router_hermes.hermes-plugin-package-02-source-tree-mirrors-installed-directory/tiiny-router/tiers.py"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UhJjQmG4cB6nraMWbGrjQL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFYE6krwkhyG2xrRosUK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012MJkcHhveBYbcpAgDFzxNm","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"rmdir tiiny-router/plugin; python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"tiiny-router/scripts/route_check.py\")\ns = p.read_text()\nold_doc = \"\"\"script and the backend cannot drift apart. Both are located relative to this\nfile, because the plugin and the checker ship side by side in two layouts —\n``plugin/`` inside a skill, ``examples/tiiny-router/`` inside an article.\n\"\"\"\nnew_doc = \"\"\"script and the backend cannot drift apart. Both sit in the plugin directory,\none level above this script, and are found relative to this file only.\n\"\"\"\nassert old_doc in s\ns = s.replace(old_doc, new_doc)\nstart = s.index(\"#: Where the plugin's shared modules\")\nend = s.index('tiers = _load(\"tiiny_tiers\"')\nnew = '''#: The plugin directory: this script lives in its ``scripts/`` folder.\n_PLUGIN_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n\n\ndef _load(name: str, filename: str):\n    \"\"\"Load a shared plugin module by path from the plugin directory.\"\"\"\n    path = _PLUGIN_DIR / filename\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(name, path)\n    if not path.exists() or spec is None or spec.loader is None:\n        raise SystemExit(\n            f\"could not find {filename}. It ships in the plugin directory: \"\n            f\"{path}\"\n        )\n    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n    return module\n\n\n'''\ns = s[:start] + new + s[end:]\np.write_text(s)\nEOF\npython3 -B test/test_installed_tree.py 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":288,"cache_read_input_tokens":59894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"e