{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFYKJJY5Wv7ASg2FWzSn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] A copy of the directory placed at an arbitrary path runs `route_check.py` successfully\n[x] A copy of the directory placed at an arbitrary path runs a read-only `tiiny_ctl.py` command that loads the tier table (e.g. `--help` or a plan dry run) without \"could not find the tier table\"\n[x] Importing the backend module from a copy at an arbitrary path loads the controller module (`ctl` is not `None`)\n[x] No lookup references `examples/`, `skill/plugin`, or `hermes-agent/plugins/delegation`\n\nAll four checklist items are done, in three commits, and `npm test` passes (4 tests).\n\n**Layout.** I renamed `skill/` to `tiiny-router/` and moved the backend modules (`__init__.py`, `plugin.yaml`, `tiers.py`, `thinking.py`) up from `plugin/` to the top of that directory. The tree is now exactly what gets installed at `$HERMES_HOME/plugins/tiiny-router/`. The controller scripts are in `scripts/`, and the skill (`SKILL.md`, `references/`, `templates/`) sits next to the backend.\n\n**Lookups.** The search lists are gone, and each file now looks in one place relative to its own location:\n- `route_check.py` loads `tiers.py` and `thinking.py` from the directory one level above it.\n- `tiiny_ctl.py` loads the tier table from `SKILL_ROOT / \"tiers.py\"`.\n- The backend's `_CTL_SPEC` looks for the controller in `scripts/` inside its own directory. Before this, a wrong path here wasn't reported: the backend just set `ctl` to `None`.\n\n**Tests.** `test/test_installed_tree.py` runs through `npm test`. It copies `tiiny-router/` to an arbitrary temp path, with a temp `HOME` and `HERMES_HOME`, then:\n1. runs `route_check.py --all` and a routing for a sample goal;\n2. runs `tiiny_ctl.py --help` (the tier table loads before the arguments are parsed, so a missing table makes it fail);\n3. imports the backend with a stand-in for its one Hermes import, and checks that `ctl` is not `None`.\n\nEach test failed before its fix. Because `HOME` is a temp directory, a lookup can't quietly fall back to a copy under `~/.hermes/hermes-agent`. I wrote this as a standalone Python script rather than with `node:test`; the spec allows that for the Python checks, and the repo has no TypeScript setup yet.\n\n**Item 4** needed no separate change. Items 1–3 removed every such path, and searching the code under `tiiny-router/` finds no `examples`, `skill/plugin` or `hermes-agent` references.\n\n**Left alone:**\n- The controller's `devices.py` lookup under `$HERMES_HOME/mesh` and its vault search. Neither one loads the tier table.\n- Old paths in `SKILL.md`, `references/` and `docs/`. The spec leaves those doc rewrites to a later ticket.\n\nI rewrote the layout section of `AGENTS.md` for the new tree and the relative-lookup rule. Notes for this attempt are in `.redeye/notes.md`, uncommitted as instructed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":964,"cache_read_input_tokens":68388,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":964},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fa7ddb5-486f-4c1d-8d10-e98d3ec44829","uuid":"f37ad517-75bc-4276-abe3-b04e971700ec","timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:43:29.170Z","request_id":"req_011ChFYKJ9cQFP6gZFRYxuh6"}
